            <ArticleTitle>The many causes of headache. Migraine, vascular, drug-induced, and more.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>67-8, 71-2, 75-6 passim</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Accurate diagnosis of headache can be challenging when the pain pattern and the source are not immediately recognized. The most common types of headache are primary (i.e., migraine, tension-type, and cluster). In addition, many secondary causes of head pain have been identified. Dr Levin reviews the major types of headache as categorized by the International Headache Society and provides a list of red flags that may signal a secondary headache.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
